-- ============================================================
-- 0031: Spell out acronyms on first use, in every course
-- ============================================================
-- Rule of thumb for all lesson content: the first time an acronym appears
-- in a course (in reading order: domains in order, lessons in order, recap
-- last), it's spelled out, e.g. "recovery time objective (RTO)". After
-- that, the bare acronym is fine. Obvious ones (IT, USB, PC, PDF, HR, CEO,
-- units like GB) are left alone.
--
-- Generated from an audit of all lesson content: 506 field edits across
-- 212 lessons. Each update only applies if the field still has the exact
-- text that was audited, so re-running this is harmless and it will never
-- overwrite a field that's been edited since.
--
-- Narration audio for changed slides is regenerated by the nightly
-- "Generate narration" GitHub Action (or run it by hand).


